Wrong (A): Substantial support refers to the nature of the modifications, not whether an audit opinion has been issued. A formal audit is not required for the modifications to be valid.
Wrong (B): Revenue sufficiency relates to going concern, not to the acceptability of accounting modifications under the modified cash basis.
