  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under the tax basis, financial statements already use IRC recognition and measurement rules. Since both the statements and the tax return follow the same rules, there are no temporary differences between book and tax amounts. The ASC 740 concept of deferred tax assets and liabilities does not apply.
Wrong (B): Recording $250,000 times the tax rate as a deferred liability applies ASC 740 GAAP logic to tax-basis statements. When both systems use the same rules, nothing needs to be deferred.
