-- Q11508: Special Purpose Frameworks [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AICPA SPF guidance and ASC 235-10-50, cash-basis statements recognize revenue when cash is received and expenses when cash is paid. Delaying $200,000 in vendor payments to January removes those expenses from the current year. Accelerating $150,000 in collections into December adds that revenue. The combined effect increases cash-basis income by $350,000.
Wrong (A): The two transactions do not offset. Delayed payments reduce expenses while accelerated collections increase revenue, both boosting income in the same direction.
Wrong (B): A $50,000 decrease incorrectly nets the two amounts. The $200,000 savings and $150,000 additional revenue both increase income, totaling $350,000.
Wrong (C): The $200,000 increase from delayed payments is correct, but accelerated collections increase income by $150,000 rather than decreasing it. Both actions raise current-year cash-basis income.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11508;

