-- Q11522: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SFAC No. 5 and ASC 606, the accrual basis recognizes revenue when earned regardless of cash receipt. Pinecrest records the $85,000 revenue and an accounts receivable in December 2025, resulting in higher revenue and higher assets. Under cash basis, no entry occurs until January 2026 collection.
Wrong (B): Accrual basis does not report higher liabilities from this transaction. The $85,000 creates a receivable (asset), not a liability. Cash basis reports no revenue in December.
Wrong (C): Both bases do not report the same revenue. Cash basis defers recognition until cash is received in January, while accrual basis records it in December when earned.
Wrong (D): The question asks about revenue and asset effects. While related expenses may be accrued, accrual basis still reports higher net income in December because the revenue recognition occurs in that period.$EXPL$
