-- Q11523: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IAS 38, development costs must be capitalized when all six criteria (TIPARA) are met, making capitalization mandatory. Under U.S. GAAP (ASC 730), research and development costs are expensed as incurred regardless of project stage or likelihood of success, creating a significant GAAP-IFRS divergence.
Wrong (A): U.S. GAAP does not permit capitalization of R&D costs (except for software development under ASC 985-20). ASC 730 requires expensing, so both frameworks do not require capitalization.
Wrong (B): IFRS explicitly distinguishes research (always expensed) from development (capitalized when criteria are met). IFRS does not require expensing all R&D costs.
